 "_": [
  "HOL-SEC-191: the Windows entire-screen share's voice redirect names voices by connection",
  "and receiver and keeps the listener's volume. Both peers Windows. a deafens, shares Screen 1",
  "with audio (redirect arms), b watches (capturer excludes the child), a un-deafens and",
  "deafens during the share, stops the share while deafened. Proof lines in a's",
  "hollow_debug.log: '[HOLLOW-VC] Voice redirect armed (N voice(s) at volumes ...)',",
  "'[HOLLOW-AU-SCREEN] VC voice redirect armed (pid=', the Volume lines during the share",
  "(on n/n receiver(s)), 'Voice redirect stopped (N voice(s) back at volumes 0.00)' and",
  "'VC voice redirect disarmed'. Audio itself is not provable by widgets. Needs a 0.14 relay.",
  "run (mini): bash scripts/pc_sync.sh sec-014; pwsh -NoProfile -File scripts/fleet.ps1 -Onboard -Fresh -Peers windows:<x>,windows:<y> -Relay hollowtest.duckdns.org; pwsh -NoProfile -File scripts/fleet.ps1 -Scenario redir_share_vc_desktop -Peers a=windows:<x>,b=windows:<y>"
 ],
 "peers": [
  "a",
  "b"
 ],
